static const unsigned char app_apps_README_md[] =
    "# cwick apps\n\nEach app is a self-contained H5 bundle und"
    "er `apps/<id>/`; `manifest.json`\nlists what the built-in"
    " app market shows. The server embeds this tree into the\n"
    "binary (see `tools/embed_web.c`) and serves it at `/apps"
    "/...` on the same\norigin as the OpenAI API, so an app ne"
    "eds no build step, no package manager and\nno CORS config"
    "uration.\n\nLayout:\n\n```\napps/\n  manifest.json          # "
    "the market catalog\n  tictactoe/             # \344\271\235\345\256\253\346\240\274\344"
    "\272\225\345\255\227\346\243\213\n    app.json             # app metadata (kept n"
    "ext to the code)\n    index.html           # entry\n    ap"
    "p.css\n    app.js\n  kart/                  # 3D \346\263\241\346\263\241\345\215\241"
    "\344\270\201\350\275\246\n    app.json\n    index.html\n    app.css\n    app.j"
    "s\n```\n\nEvery app asks the model through `POST /v1/system"
    "one`; the chat tab keeps\nusing `/v1/chat/completions`. E"
    "very request an app makes is same-origin \342\200\224\nthere is no"
    " configurable external endpoint. The resident model is d"
    "iscovered\nfrom `GET /v1/models` and re-discovered after "
    "a server-side switch, so the\ndecision adapter always fol"
    "lows the checkpoint that is actually loaded.\n\nTo add an "
    "app: create `apps/<id>/`, add its entry to `manifest.jso"
    "n`, then run\n`make` (which builds and runs the C generat"
    "or `tools/embed_web`) and restart\n`cwick serve --web`.\n\n"
    "## Where an app keeps its data\n\n**Not** in `localStorage"
    "` alone. The server owns the databases in `~/.cwick/apps"
    "/`\n(`--store DIR`, or `$CWICK_STORE`): **one file per ap"
    "p**, `<id>.db`, plus `auth.db`\nfor the server's own API "
    "keys. A `--store` path that exists as a file or ends in\n"
    "`.db`/`.sqlite` still means one shared database \342\200\224 the "
    "old layout \342\200\224 and every\napp's rows then live in that on"
    "e file behind their `app_id`.\n\nRun from a checkout, `--s"
    "tore ./apps` puts each app's database right next to its\n"
    "code (`apps/tictactoe.db`, `apps/kart.db`). That is deli"
    "berate and safe:\n`tools/embed_web.c` skips every databas"
    "e suffix when it walks `apps/`, so a\nrunning server's fi"
    "les are never compiled into the binary, and `.gitignore`"
    "\nkeeps them out of a commit.\n\nThree generic collections "
    "per app, all behind the same login as the model:\n\n```\nGE"
    "T    /v1/store                          layout, per-app "
    "row counts, file size\nGET    /v1/store?app=<id>         "
    "        that app's own database\nGET    /v1/apps/<id>/sta"
    "te                every key            -> {\"items\":[...]"
    "}\nGET    /v1/apps/<id>/state?key=K          one value   "
    "         -> {\"value\":<json>}\nPUT    /v1/apps/<id>/state "
    "               {\"key\":K,\"value\":V} or {\"values\":{...}}\nD"
    "ELETE /v1/apps/<id>/state?key=K\nGET    /v1/apps/<id>/eve"
    "nts?game_id=G&limit=N\nPOST   /v1/apps/<id>/events       "
    "        {\"game_id\",\"seq\",\"kind\",\"payload\"}\nGET    /v1/ap"
    "ps/<id>/games?limit=N        newest first\nPUT    /v1/app"
    "s/<id>/games                {\"game_id\",\"started_at\",\"end"
    "ed_at\",\"outcome\",\"moves\"}\nDELETE /v1/apps/<id>/games?gam"
    "e_id=G      the game and its events\n```\n\nEvery value and"
    " payload must be JSON; it is stored as the exact text th"
    "at\narrived and handed back verbatim, so an app never has"
    " to match a schema the\nserver invented. `<id>` is `[A-Za"
    "-z0-9_-]{1,64}` \342\200\224 checked before it reaches\nsqlite \342\200\224"
    " and limits are 1 MiB per value / payload and 5000 rows "
    "per read.\n\nWhy a server-side store rather than `localSto"
    "rage`:\n\n- \"clear site data\", a private window or a secon"
    "d browser profile would erase a\n  match history the mode"
    "l produced;\n- the phone that scanned the QR is a differe"
    "nt browser and must see the same\n  scoreboard and histor"
    "y;\n- an app's history is worth keeping after the tab is "
    "gone.\n\n`apps/tictactoe` uses all three collections: `sta"
    "te` for the scoreboard, `games`\nfor one row per match (`"
    "started_at`, `ended_at`, `outcome`, `moves`) and\n`events"
    "` for one row per move (`kind` = `human`/`ai`, payload ="
    " board snapshot,\nprompt with the per-cell tactical facts"
    ", the model's full probability\ndistribution as `probs`, "
    "raw model answer, parsed move, latency, usage). The\nrigh"
    "t-hand column's **\345\216\206\345\217\262\345\233\236\346\224\276** tab reads them back and"
    " replays a finished game\nstep by step.\n\n`apps/kart` uses"
    " the same three: `games` for one row per run (`moves` = "
    "obstacles\nthe model placed), `events` for `kind` = `spaw"
    "n`/`hit`/`lap`/`end` (payload = the\nobstacle type, the p"
    "osition on the strip, the kart's speed, the model's late"
    "ncy,\nits raw answer, plus the variation `seed`, pressure"
    " `focus` and decision\n`entropy`) and `state` for the bes"
    "t score and a lifetime tally. Every spawn is a\nmodel dec"
    "ision, so the replay shows what the model actually said "
    "for each\nobstacle rather than a number from a generator."
    "\n\n## Which apps decide, and through which endpoint\n\nBoth"
    " hosted apps ask the model to choose, and both call `POS"
    "T /v1/systemone`.\nThe chat tab is a different consumer: "
    "it uses `/v1/chat/completions`, because a\nconversation i"
    "s generated text, not a choice among options.\n\n- **tic-t"
    "ac-toe** \342\200\224 the human plays X first. Each machine move "
    "is a `choice`\n  over the empty cells, and the question i"
    "s explicitly *which cell gives O the\n  greatest probabil"
    "ity of winning*. The state carries the board and one lin"
    "e of\n  tactical facts per empty cell (immediate win, for"
    "ced block, winning replies,\n  open lines). Those are fac"
    "ts, not a ranked list: the old wording \342\200\224 \"win, else\n  "
    "block, else centre, else corner\" \342\200\224 was a local rule dr"
    "essed up as a question\n  and was removed. `fallbackMove("
    ")` remains, but only for a failed request.\n- **kart** \342\200"
    "\224 a 12-way `choice` of obstacle kind and lane, asked in "
    "real time\n  while the kart is moving. The question now a"
    "sks for *maximum difficulty*; the\n  previous \"leave room"
    " for the player to react\" was the opposite of the goal.\n"
    "\nWhat stays local is what a letter cannot express: the k"
    "art's obstacle distance\nis derived from speed (and tight"
    "ens with the lap, above a reaction floor). The\nmodel dec"
    "ides *what*, the app computes *where* \342\200\224 and an app nev"
    "er substitutes a\nlocally generated obstacle for a model "
    "decision.\n\nAny app that caches a model id must handle a "
    "switch on the server side: a 400\nwhose text says the mod"
    "el is no longer served drops the cached id, rediscovers\n"
    "the resident model and retries once. `GET /v1/systemone`"
    " answers which family,\nprompt grammar and letter set are"
    " live, so a client can check rather than\ninfer.\n\n## The "
    "win-probability readout in `apps/tictactoe`\n\n`cellFacts("
    ")` computes, for each empty cell and each mark, whether "
    "the move\nwins immediately, whether it blocks the opponen"
    "t's immediate win, how many\nwinning replies remain, and "
    "how many lines are still open. It never ranks or\npicks a"
    " cell \342\200\224 it is the same information a human counts, ren"
    "dered into the\nstate and into each option's description."
    " The endpoint's softmax over the\noption letters is the m"
    "odel's distribution over \"which cell wins most\"; its\narg"
    "max is the move.\n\nThe right-hand column draws one bar pe"
    "r empty cell, highlights the cell\nactually played, and s"
    "hows the human's own tactical facts on their move, so\nbo"
    "th sides of the game have a decision trail. The bars are"
    " a readout of one\nprefill, **not** a Monte-Carlo win rat"
    "e, and the heading says so: calling them\na simulated win"
    " percentage would be a claim the endpoint cannot make.\n\n"
    "## The model decides the obstacles in `apps/kart`\n\n`pump"
    "Agent()` runs once per frame while racing and keeps at m"
    "ost one request in\nflight and a two-deep queue of decisi"
    "ons, because a kart covers ~13 m in the\ntime a 320B mode"
    "l takes to answer \342\200\224 so the model is asked about a stre"
    "tch of\ntrack 45\342\200\22395 m ahead rather than about the next "
    "frame.\n\nThe question is a 12-way `choice` at `/v1/system"
    "one`: four obstacle kinds times\nthree lanes, one letter "
    "each. The model never writes a lane offset or a\ndistance"
    " \342\200\224 numbers it would have to generate token by token, a"
    "nd then be\nrepaired when it wrote prose around them. The"
    " distance is derived locally from\nthe kart's speed, whic"
    "h also keeps the road readable: the player sees where th"
    "e\nthing will be, not just what kind it is. The state is "
    "one line of English facts: lap, speed, hits, obstacles a"
    "head,\nspawned so far, difficulty level, which side of th"
    "e strip is up, a variation\nseed and a pressure point. Ev"
    "ery byte is prefill on every obstacle, which is\nwhy the "
    "option labels are short English and the Chinese names st"
    "ay in the\nsidebar.\n\n**Real-time random decisions.** The "
    "readout is deterministic for a fixed\nprompt, and a fixed"
    " A..L order would put the model's letter bias on the sam"
    "e\nobstacle every time. Each request therefore Fisher-Yat"
    "es shuffles the twelve\noptions (`criteria` is an ordered"
    " object on the server, so member order becomes\nthe lette"
    "rs), draws a fresh variation seed and one of six pressur"
    "e points, and\nasks for the hardest obstacle it can choos"
    "e. The variation lives in the\n*question*, never on the r"
    "oad: the seed, pressure point and the normalised\nentropy"
    " of the resulting distribution are shown in the sidebar "
    "and written to\nthe sqlite `agent`/`spawn` events, so it "
    "is auditable rather than hidden.\n\n**There is no local ge"
    "nerator behind it.** This is the requirement, not an\nacc"
    "ident: an empty queue means an empty road, the HUD says "
    "`\346\250\241\345\236\213\347\246\273\347\272\277 \302\267 \346\232\202\344\270\215\346\224\276\350\267\257\351\232\234`,\nand the sidebar's `\345\267"
    "\262\346\224\276\350\267\257\351\232\234` can never exceed the model's successful deci"
    "sions.\nThe alternative \342\200\224 silently inventing obstacles "
    "when the model is slow \342\200\224 makes\nthe statistics a lie an"
    "d hides a broken integration behind a playable game.\n\nTh"
    "ree traps this app has already hit, all worth rememberin"
    "g:\n\n- the model id must be the one the server advertises"
    " (`GET /v1/models`), never a\n  literal \342\200\224 an invented n"
    "ame is a 400 and the model is never asked at all;\n- `ens"
    "ureModel()` returns the discovery promise from `resolveM"
    "odel()`, which\n  caches the in-flight `GET /v1/models` s"
    "o several obstacles spawned in one\n  frame share a singl"
    "e lookup. An empty answer must not be cached, or one col"
    "d\n  start would leave the game without obstacles for the"
    " whole run. Failures like\n  that are invisible on screen"
    " \342\200\224 the road is just empty for a moment \342\200\224 so the\n  mo"
    "del state is exposed under `?debug`;\n- a model id cached"
    " before a server-side switch is refused on *every* call\n"
    "  (\"model `x` is not served by this endpoint\"). A 400 wi"
    "th that text now drops\n  the id, rediscovers the residen"
    "t model and retries once;\n- one decision is one prefill,"
    " and the endpoint takes a generation slot: on this\n  sin"
    "gle-slot server an obstacle decision queues behind a cha"
    "t turn. That is why\n  the queue is only two deep and why"
    " an empty queue is shown as an empty road\n  rather than "
    "papered over.\n\n## The 3D renderer in `apps/kart`\n\nNo Web"
    "GL, no library: the kart is a small triangle rasteriser "
    "on a 2D canvas.\nEach frame it pushes ~700 triangles into"
    " one buffer (track quads, curbs, centre\nand edge lines, "
    "quarter-lap gates, obstacle boxes, the kart), sorts them"
    "\nfar-to-near and fills them. Three details carry the who"
    "le thing:\n\n- **camera space is forward-positive.** `toCa"
    "m()` dots a point with (right, up,\n  forward) from the e"
    "ye, so z > 0 means in front; the projection divides by z"
    " and\n  a Sutherland\342\200\223Hodgman clip against `z >= NEAR` t"
    "rims the polygons that straddle\n  the camera. An earlier"
    " version used the OpenGL convention (forward = \342\210\222z) in "
    "the\n  view matrix while the clip assumed +z, which culle"
    "d the entire world;\n- **normals are normalised before sh"
    "ading.** The cross product of a quad's edges\n  has lengt"
    "h = its area (a road segment is 8.8 m by 1.7 m, so |n| \342"
    "\211\210 15); using\n  that directly as a brightness factor sat"
    "urates every large quad to white,\n  which is exactly how"
    " one build turned the strip into a white slab;\n- **the c"
    "amera's up vector is the surface normal**, so the horizo"
    "n rolls with the\n  strip instead of staying level with t"
    "he world. That is what makes the flip\n  readable rather "
    "than a floating camera over a twisted ribbon;\n- **road t"
    "exture must be indexed by world position, not by segment"
    " index.** The\n  banding and centre dashes were picked wi"
    "th `i & 1` over the window the camera\n  draws; because t"
    "hat window moves with the kart, the pattern moved with i"
    "t and\n  the road looked painted on the lens \342\200\224 93 km/h "
    "and nothing on the surface said\n  so. Snapping the segme"
    "nts to a world grid (`first = floor(u / du)`) makes the\n"
    "  stripes stream past. A chase cam also needs a spring: "
    "with the eye an exact\n  function of the kart's position,"
    " acceleration shows nothing; a few metres of\n  lag, a 2 "
    "cm bob and a focal kick with speed are what \"driving\" lo"
    "oks like.\n\nThe track is a parametric M\303\266bius strip, `S(u"
    ", v) = C(u) + A(u)\302\267v` with\n`A(u) = cos(u/2)\302\267radial + s"
    "in(u/2)\302\267up`, so after one lap the across direction is\nr"
    "eversed \342\200\224 one side, one surface, and the gates built i"
    "n that frame arrive\nupside down half a lap later.\n\nThe s"
    "trip is drawn in two zones: the near ~1.3 rad at full de"
    "tail (banding,\nkerbs, dashes, painted start/twist bands)"
    " and the rest out to 4.4 rad as one\ncoarse quad per 0.08"
    " rad plus a bright rim. Without the far zone a M\303\266bius t"
    "rack\nis indistinguishable from a banked ring \342\200\224 you onl"
    "y ever see the ten metres under\nthe kart. The rim is wha"
    "t carries the shape: a M\303\266bius strip is recognised by it"
    "s\nsingle continuous edge.\n\nA chase camera sits *inside* "
    "the twist, which is exactly why the app also draws a\nsma"
    "ll inset: the whole loop from outside the ring, with up-"
    "facing faces teal and\ndown-facing faces violet so the ha"
    "lf-twist shows as a colour flip, plus the\nkart's dot. It"
    "s projection is written separately from the main camera "
    "on\npurpose \342\200\224 the main camera is a per-frame function o"
    "f the kart and must not be\ndisturbed by a 140-pixel diag"
    "ram. `?debug` exposes `window.__kart` (`G`, `AGENT`,\n`tr"
    "is()`, `frameAt`) so a headless run can tell \"zero trian"
    "gles\" from \"triangles\nbehind the camera\".\n\n## Sharing on"
    " the LAN\n\n`cwick serve --lan` binds all interfaces (no a"
    "uth/TLS; trusted Wi-Fi only) and\nprints e.g. `LAN share:"
    " http://192.168.71.84:8001/apps/tictactoe/`. **Every app"
    "\nhere carries a \345\210\206\344\272\253 / \344\272\214\347\273\264\347\240\201 button** \342\200\224 it calls"
    " `GET /v1/share?app=<id>` and\nrenders the answer through"
    " `GET /v1/share/qr?text=<url>`; scanning the PNG opens\nt"
    "hat app standalone on a phone. Two things are worth know"
    "ing:\n\n- **the `?app=` is not optional for a new app.** T"
    "he server's default is\n  `tictactoe`, so an app that for"
    "gets it will happily hand out a QR for somebody\n  else's"
    " page. The id is charset-checked before it reaches `prin"
    "tf`.\n- **`shareable:false` is a real answer**, returned "
    "with a `warning` when the\n  listener is loopback-only or"
    " has no LAN IPv4. The sheet shows the reason and\n  the `"
    "--lan` hint instead of a code that would not resolve.\n\n\n"
    "With `--lan`, cwick forces single-user login, so an unau"
    "thenticated phone is\nredirected to `/login?next=/apps/<i"
    "d>/` and returns to the app after the\npassword \342\200\224 which"
    " is why every share note says the first open needs it. T"
    "he apps\nare responsive (tested at 390 px) and do not nee"
    "d the main console shell when\nopened from that URL \342\200\224 t"
    "he kart opens straight into its race because that is all"
    "\nit does.\n"
    "\000";

